## Materials & Solution Preparation

A polysulfone (PSf) c...

[2026-06-19 18:17:33] final_report: asting solution was prepared at a concentration of **17 wt%** in PolarClean solvent, with a total solution volume of **1000 µL**. The solution was mixed and heated at **60°C** to ensure complete polymer dissolution and homogeneity.

## Membrane Casting

The polymer solution was blade-cast onto the substrate at a controlled pulling speed of **1 mm/s**. Following casting, the membrane coupon was exposed to a **laminar dry nitrogen purge** for **450 seconds (7.5 minutes)** prior to bath immersion. This nitrogen blow step was employed to control surface humidity and promote selective evaporation of the solvent at the film surface, which can influence the resulting membrane morphology and skin layer formation.

## Phase Inversion (NIPS Bath)

After the evaporation period, the cast film was immersed into a non-solvent bath maintained at **5°C**. The membrane was allowed to undergo phase separation in the bath for **1800 seconds (30 minutes)** to ensure complete precipitation and solidification of the polymer matrix.

