## Membrane Casting

The polymer solution was blade-cast onto the substrate at a controlled pulling speed of **1 mm/s**. Following casting, the membrane coupon was exposed to a **laminar dry nitrogen purge** for **310 seconds** prior to bath immersion. This nitrogen blow step was employed to displace ambient humidity from the film surface and control the early-stage solvent-nonsolvent exchange dynamics.

## Phase Inversion (NIPS Bath)

After the pre-immersion exposure period, the cast film was immersed into a non-solvent bath maintained at **5°C**. The membrane was allowed to undergo phase separation in the bath for **1800 seconds (30 minutes)**, during which the solvent-nonsolvent exchange drove polymer precipitation and membrane solidification.

