[2026-06-19 22:41:19] final_report: ope solution was prepared at a concentration of **17 wt%** in PolarClean solvent, with a total volume of **1000 µL**. The solution was mixed and heated at **60°C** to ensure complete polymer dissolution and homogeneity.

## Membrane Casting

The polymer solution was blade-cast onto the substrate at a controlled pulling speed of **1 mm/s**. Following casting, the membrane coupon was exposed to a **laminar dry nitrogen purge** for **275 seconds** prior to bath immersion. This nitrogen blow step was employed to displace ambient humidity from the film surface and control the early-stage evaporation environment.

## Phase Separation (NIPS Bath)

After the pre-immersion period, the cast film was immersed into a non-solvent (water) bath maintained at a reduced temperature of **5°C**. The membrane was allowed to undergo phase separation in the bath for **1800 seconds (30 minutes)**, during which solvent-nonsolvent exchange drove the formation of the final asymmetric membrane structure.

