After the pre-immersion period, the cast membrane was immersed into the non-solvent (NIPS) coagulation bath, maintained at a reduced temperature of **5°C**. The membrane remained in the bath for **1800 seconds (30 minutes)** to allow complete phase separation and membrane solidification.

